    "body": "I don't think we need to specially mangle the names of _functions_ that use the vector calling convention.  While arguably useful for function multi-versioning and the `[[gnu::target_version]]` attribute in particular, this is orthogonal to C++ overload resolution.\r\n\r\nWe do need to mangle _function pointer types_ that use the vector calling convention, whether or not the function taking the parameter itself uses the vector calling convention, to allow overloading a function that takes arguments with different ABIs.",
    "created_at": "2024-02-02T14:05:43Z",
    "updated_at": "2024-02-02T14:05:44Z",
