    "body": "ABI tags (B) are used for the GNU abi_tag extension, which uses a string that is entirely under the control of a library author.  It is probably wrong to use for architecture-specific features, and it does not fix my original example since it cannot be used on unnamed entities.\r\n\r\nI was originally thinking of using a vendor-defined pointer qualifier as defined in [5.1.5.1 Qualified types](https://itanium-cxx-abi.github.io/cxx-abi/abi.html#mangle.qualified-type), but the closest existing thing to what I'm asking for is the definition of Dx in [5.1.5.3 Function types](https://itanium-cxx-abi.github.io/cxx-abi/abi.html#mangle.function-type).  We may need upstream guidance.",
